fixture zone1_03_optional_ladder_chain
doc BUILD.md s15 "a 10-bounce chain across the zone 1 spike pit is possible at 4 bounces per second"; docs/adr/0019 Decision 5. The optional path stitched end to end, with no pause between its two halves: the ladder up from the main hall (03_optional_ladder, ticks 0 to 122), landing on the upper level at x 399 u with the run held, then 4 more ticks of run, a ground dash on tick 127 (x 435 u, as 03_pogo_chain_route dashes at x 434 u from the spawn), the hop into the dash-jump and ten bounces at 4 a second, 15 ticks apart, each at the dash-jump's full 20 u/f, from x 786 u to x 3486 u. The tenth arc lands on the low hall (tick 296, x 3826 u, 242 u past the tunnel's end at 3584 u). Until this fixture nothing proved that a player arriving from the ladder has the run-up for the chain: the exit at x 399 u leaves 36 u of floor-run before the dash at 435 u.
